<section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence review · Sep 23, 2026</p><h1>Mangools API & data review: hands-on product evidence vs documented API</h1>
<div class="notice"><strong>Boundary:</strong> our prior hands-on run used Mangools product interfaces. Search Data Bench has not authenticated the current account against the Mangools API, so API entitlement, SDB-B01 cost and quota remain UNRESOLVED.</div>
<h2>What we tested</h2><p>On September 21, 2026, the prior frozen test used Mangools Free+. KWFinder accepted and exported 25/25 frozen keywords. SiteProfiler and LinkMiner completed all four frozen-domain checks.</p>
<p>SERPChecker returned 17, 7 and 9 organic rows for the first three fixed queries. The remaining three queries were recorded as UNAVAILABLE / LIMIT after the observed lookup allowance was exhausted. SERPWatcher accepted all 25 keywords, but rank values had not returned by the final verification poll.</p>
<h2>What Mangools documents now</h2><p>Mangools publishes an official API reference with API-key authentication through the <code>x-access-token</code> header and a machine-readable OpenAPI specification. It also documents an AI Search Watcher API for managing monitors, models, prompts and settings around AI-search visibility.</p>
